    "root_cause_explanation": "The low ML log loss of 0.3720 in Fold 2 is NOT caused by feature leakage, code error, or lookahead bias. Rather, it is the empirical consequence of Formula 1's most statistically one-sided season in history. Max Verstappen won 19 of 22 races (86.4%), and Red Bull won 21 of 22 (95.5%). Trained on 2021-2022, the LightGBM model recognized Red Bull's overwhelming aerodynamic superiority, which was strongly reflected in pre-race features (driver rolling 5 win rate, constructor qualifying pace delta to pole, and starting grid position). The model consistently assigned 65% to 85% win probability to Verstappen. Because Verstappen repeatedly won, the race-level log loss on these 19 events was near zero (-ln(0.80) = 0.223). In only 3 races did an upset occur (Perez in Jeddah/Baku, Sainz in Singapore). Crucially, this ultra-low loss is idiosyncratic to the 2023 monopoly and does NOT represent generalizable performance in competitive seasons, as evidenced by Fold 1 (2022) where pure ML suffered a log loss of 2.1853.",
